But wait: "Si detectas una falta de definición, infórmala antes de editar." There are indeed missing definitions:
1. DS-2 marks cells E but does NOT formulate a per-cell falsifiable question with a numeric multiplier ("el mecanismo multiplica el coste mínimo de X por al menos …"). The ORDEN §1 says "Pregunta falsable: la que DS-2 formule para cada celda E". DS-2 didn't formulate any such per-cell question. This is a genuine gap. I should report it.

2. The "coste mínimo de X para alcanzar una probabilidad de éxito dada" is not uniquely defined: for several attack mechanisms, the cost model in MODELO gives formulas for specific quantities (retention region, coverage cost, first-passage probability), but not a unified "minimum cost to reach success probability p". The model doesn't define how cost maps to success probability except for A1/A2 (first passage) and A3 (coverage cliff). There's no explicit mapping for A4/A5/A7. Only cells E: A3 (F1+F2+F4 and M1 weak), A4 (M1/F4), A5 (O4), A7 (F3), A1 (O2), A6 (O2), A9 (F4), A10 (F1/F4/F5), A12 (W). Hmm.

Actually, I should not over-engineer. Let me re-read the order carefully.

ORDEN-DS3 §1: "Objetivo único: calcular, para los ataques y mecanismos que DS-2 marque E, el coste mínimo absoluto de X para alcanzar una probabilidad de éxito dada, en cada dimensión del marco, en B0, B1 y con cada candidato; y el cociente frente al coste del honesto."

§2 Method: closed formulas + independent MC; parameters from a file with labels; outputs CSV + INFORME.md with per attack "coste mínimo en B0 → en B1 → con cada candidato", ratio to honest, and dominant parameter (sensitivity). Pkg.test() with the check cases; run.jl reproducible.

Ratificación: "Los siete casos de su §4 son la regresión obligatoria de Pkg.test(). Además de su tabla por ataque, entrega una tabla por mecanismo con el Δ de coste absoluto de X y el coste para el honesto en los escenarios del §3".

So the deliverables:
- Julia project in DS3 with Project.toml, Manifest.toml, src/, test/, bench/, run.jl, resultados/, INFORME.md.
- Closed-form implementation + Monte Carlo of the same model, matching within declared statistical error for the check cases.
- Scenario parameter file with labels and provenance; declared sweeps; fixed non-consecutive StableRNGs seeds.
