  So the check cases are implementable.

G4. The "Monte Carlo independente del mismo modelo" must match closed formulas in the check cases. But some check cases are exact arithmetic, not probabilistic (α*, B(ε), coverage step, BP formula). Only cases 2 (first passage) and 3 (retention P(B=0)) are stochastic. And perhaps case 5's φ_γ (hypergeometric) and case 6. Monte Carlo would be for the first-passage walk and the retention process. For the rest, MC isn't meaningful; I'll implement MC where the model is stochastic and note the rest are deterministic.

