`validar_alpha` error_max = 0.34. My `validar_alpha` uses the wrong g formula. `alpha_estrella` is the root of which reparto? Let me reconsider.

MODELO §2.1: `α* = (η_h − η_a·β_d − (η_h+η_a)·β_x)/(η_h+η_a)`. P-CLAVE note says this corresponds to the alternative reparto where β_d abandons the public: `deriva_alt = η_a(α+βd+βx) − η_h(1−α−βd−βx)`. Setting to zero and solving for α:
η_a α + η_a βd + η_a βx = η_h(1−α−βd−βx)
α(η_a+η_h) = η_h − η_h βd − η_h βx − η_a βd − η_a βx
α = (η_h − (η_h+η_a) βd − (η_h+η_a) βx)/(η_h+η_a)
= (η_h − (η_h+η_a)(βd+βx))/(η_h+η_a).
But MODELO's formula is `(η_h − η_a βd − (η_h+η_a) βx)/(η_h+η_a)`. These differ in the βd coefficient: η_a vs (η_h+η_a). With η=1, MODELO: (1 − βd − 2βx)/2. deriva_alt root: (1 − 2βd − 2βx)/2. So they differ.

Hmm. Let me re-read P-PRESTAMO §1: g = η_a(α+βd+βx) − η_h(1−α−βx). Setting g=0:
η_a α + η_a βd + η_a βx = η_h − η_h α − η_h βx
α(η_a+η_h) = η_h − η_a βd − (η_h+η_a) βx
α* = (η_h − η_a βd − (η_h+η_a) βx)/(η_h+η_a). ✓ This matches MODELO. Good.
So α* is the root of `g = η_a(α+βd+βx) − η_h(1−α−βx)` (the "encargo" reparto, where βd stays in public). Good.

The P-CLAVE note claimed the formula corresponds to `deriva_alt`; that's an error in P-CLAVE's comment (or a different accounting). Regardless, MODELO's α* is the root of the MODELO §2.1 g, which in my code is `deriva(Reparto) = mu_privada - mu_publica = ηa(α+βd+βx) − ηh(1−α−βx)`. So `validar_alpha` should check `g = ηa*(a+βd+βx) - ηh*(1-a-βx) = 0`, not the alt. Let me fix validar_alpha. With ηh=1: g = ηa(a+βd+βx) - (1-a-βx). At a=α*: should be 0.

Let me verify: a = (1 − ηa βd − (1+ηa) βx)/(1+ηa) [with ηh=1]. 
g = ηa a + ηa βd + ηa βx − 1 + a + βx = a(ηa+1) + ηa βd + βx(ηa+1) − 1 = (1 − ηa βd − (1+ηa)βx) + ηa βd + (1+ηa)βx − 1 = 0. ✓

